From fee03cfa0168f7e55d1fabcd9a86504838b575d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:13:28 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Qiwi Browser branding

Rebrand the user-visible product name and launcher icon to "Qiwi Browser",
following cromite's Cromite-Branding.patch for the Android pieces only.

Renamed:
- chrome/app/theme/chromium/BRANDING: PRODUCT_* = "Qiwi Browser",
  COMPANY_* = "Qiwi Browser Authors" (chrome://version,
  version_info::GetProductName()).
- res_chromium_base/values/channel_constants.xml: app_name (launcher label,
  via @string/app_name in AndroidManifest.xml), bookmark/search/quick-action
  widget titles.
- android_chrome_strings.grd (233 occurrences) and browser_ui_strings.grd
  (36): "Chrome"/"Chromium"/"Google Chrome" in message text that names this
  app -> "Qiwi Browser" (About, FRE "Welcome to ...", notification
  rationale, settings, sign-in, safety check, ...). <ph> placeholders, their
  examples, desc/meaning attributes and message names are unchanged.
  IDS_LEGAL_INFORMATION_SUMMARY no longer claims "Google LLC", and
  IDS_STORAGE_MANAGEMENT_ACTIVITY_LABEL drops the "Google" prefix (as in
  cromite). Changed messages lose their translations and fall back to
  English (fallback_to_english="true").
- Launcher icon (res_chromium_base): app_icon.png, layered_app_icon.png,
  layered_app_icon_background.png at all densities rendered from
  chromium-orange-theme.svg with the same geometry as upstream (52dp logo
  on the 108dp canvas; full-bleed sectors with an 18dp ring radius for the
  round icon); layered_app_icon_foreground.xml is now a VectorDrawable with
  the ring and core paths; themed_app_icon.xml is the monochrome
  silhouette.
- res_chromium fre_product_logo.png and product_logo_name.png (FRE,
  lightweight FRE, payment sheet) use the new logo / "Qiwi Browser".

Deliberately unchanged: package name org.chromium.chrome, resource and
class names, internals, user agent; "Chrome Web Store", ChromeOS,
Chromecast, Chromebook, "Chrome & ChromeOS Additional Terms of Service",
"Chrome Help Center", "Chrome Dino", chrome:// URLs; strings outside the
two Android grds (desktop grdp/WebUI strings).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
